SWEET BATTERY GAUGE PUBLISH (patch 0395, oriole upstream port Step 2; the old oriole 0153 re-seated on upstream's sweet_chg_i2c / sweet_thermal, old 0148 reader dropped): SweetBattery (patch 0061, the iOS IOPMPowerSource) publishes the MAX77759 fuel gauge's real state of charge on gs101 instead of the static 100 % fallback. The thermal thread (patch 0336, every boot, sweetthermal=0 turns it off) adds, at most every 30 s and only after a good temperature sample, one read set through the new sweet_chg_fg_batt() (bsd/dev/sweet_chg_i2c.c): FG 0x36 reg 0x06 RepSOC (1/256 %) and reg 0x09 VCell (78.125 uV/LSB), the same registers and conversions mon_row (0298/0307) and i2c_g_fg (0284) already read, both on the i2c_rd_slave_ok allowlist, same guards and TH_RD_* codes as sweet_chg_fg_sample (a failed read stops the bus, as for every read since 0284). A set with VCell outside 2800..4600 mV or RepSOC > 102 % is not published (GAP once). sweet_batt_get() hands SweetBattery the last set (RepSOC, VCell, the sample's FG Current in mA, age). SweetBattery's existing 10 s fallback timer publishes it: percent = RepSOC rounded, External/Charging = Current > +50 mA (old 0153 rule), SweetBatteryFuelGauge = true, SweetBatterySOCEstimated = false; before the first set the static fallback stays (100 %, never 0 %); after a set older than 120 s the last values stay with SweetBatteryStale = true. Log: `SWEET BATTERY: MAX77759 fuel gauge RepSOC (patch 0395), N% ...` once on the mode change. READS ONLY: no new chip or controller register, no write. No new boot-arg. Applies after 0394.

